success: true
exit_code: 0
----- stdout -----
Create a specification with its root and Glossary sections

Usage: slcr init [OPTIONS] [FILE]

Arguments:
  [FILE]
          The requirements file to create: `.yaml`, `.yml`, `.json`, or `.toml`. It must not exist yet
          
          [default: SPEC.slcr.yml]

Options:
      --name <NAME>
          The specification's name, e.g. `todo-api`. Defaults to the file's name without its extension and any `.slcr` or `.spec`, or, for `SPEC.slcr.*`, to the name of its directory

      --title <TITLE>
          The root Section's title. Defaults to the specification's name

      --enable-colors <ENABLE_COLORS>
          Whether to color the output

          Possible values:
          - always: Always color the output
          - never:  Never color the output
          - auto:   Detect whether the terminal is a tty before deciding to color
          
          [default: auto]

      --log-level <LOG_LEVEL>
          Sets the maximum log level. Defaults to INFO. Options are 'trace', 'debug', 'info', 'warn', 'error', and 'off'. 'off' implies no logger will occur. Options are case-insensitive
          
          [env: LOG_LEVEL=]
          [default: info]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

----- stderr -----
